---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import CodeWindow from "../components/CodeWindow.astro";
import PNotes from "../components/PNotes.astro";
import freezing from "../img/freezing-man.png";
import spongy from "../img/problem-solution.jpg";
import MainThread from "../components/MainThread.astro";
import WhoWins from "../components/WhoWins.astro";
const { playful = true } = Astro.props;
---

<p-slide layout="center" autoplay timing="550">
  <h2 gradient>The Freezing problem</h2>
  <p-fragment>
    <Image
      src={freezing}
      alt="A man frozen in a block of ice"
      style="--size: 7em"
    />
  </p-fragment>
</p-slide>
<p-slide>
  <h4 layout="center" gradient style="margin-block-end: 0.5em">
    The Event Loop
  </h4>
  <figure>
    <img
      src="/img/event-loop.gif"
      alt="Animation of the JavaScript event loop moving tasks from the queues to the call stack"
      style="--size: 8em; border-radius: 0.3em"
    />
    <figcaption>
      <cite>
        <a
          href="https://dev.to/arslanyounis/how-javascript-event-loop-works-5604"
          target="_blank"
        >
          credits: Arslan Younis
        </a>
      </cite>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <PNotes>
    Event Loop, one turn:
    <p>1. Run one task (a script, a click handler, a setTimeout callback)</p>
    <p>2. Run ALL microtasks (promise callbacks, queueMicrotask)</p>
    <p>3. Maybe render: rAF callbacks, style, layout, paint</p>
    <p>
      The point for this talk: rendering only happens between tasks, so a long
      task delays every frame and every input.
    </p>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>
<p-slide>
  <h1 layout="center" gradient="sub">
    BUT
  </h1>
</p-slide>
<p-slide autoplay timing="800">
  <h4 layout="center" gradient="sub" style="margin-block-end: 0.5em">
    The Synchronous code
  </h4>
  <p-fragment timing-start="900">
    <CodeWindow is:raw file="heavy-task.js" lang="js" scale={0.76} indent={6}>
      const heavyTask = () => {
        for (let i = 0; i < 10000000000; i++) {
          //do something useful
        }
      };
    </CodeWindow>
  </p-fragment>
  <p-fragment timing-start="1400">
    <h4 layout="center" gradient="sub" style="margin-block-start: 0.5em">
      blocks the main thread!
    </h4>
  </p-fragment>
  {playful && (
    <>
      <p-fragment frozen-page no-autoplay>
        <span role="img" aria-label="Fake browser dialog: Page Unresponsive">
          <b>Page Unresponsive</b>
          <span>
            You can wait for it to become responsive or exit the page.
          </span>
          <span dialog-buttons aria-hidden="true">
            <span>Exit page</span>
            <span>Wait</span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </p-fragment>
      <MainThread
        mood="🥶"
        line="did you see that? I was frozen"
        frozen="3,000 ms"
        no-autoplay
      />
    </>
  )}
  <PNotes>
    <p>
      Next click is the fake freeze: the deck greys out and a "Page
      Unresponsive" dialog shows up. Act surprised, stare at the laptop, sigh,
      wait 2 seconds. Then click: the Main Thread complains.
    </p>
    <p>It is CSS only: the deck never really blocks, arrows keep working.</p>
  </PNotes>
</p-slide>
{playful ? (
  <WhoWins
    round={1}
    question="Which one keeps the page responsive?"
    winner="none"
    verdict="Nobody wins: both run on the main thread"
  >
    <CodeWindow is:raw slot="a" file="a.js" lang="js" dense>
        btn.onclick = async () => {
          await new Promise((ok) => {
            heavyTask();
            ok();
          });
        };
      </CodeWindow>
    <CodeWindow is:raw slot="b" file="b.js" lang="js" dense>
        btn.onclick = () => {
          setTimeout(heavyTask, 0);
        };
      </CodeWindow>
    <PNotes slot="notes">
      <p>Show of hands: A? B? Pause, let them argue.</p>
      <p>
        A: the Promise executor runs synchronously, right now. "async" is not
        "parallel": the click handler blocks for the whole loop.
      </p>
      <p>
        B: setTimeout only postpones it. The click handler returns, then the
        next macrotask is heavyTask, on the same thread → frozen again.
      </p>
      <p>The punchline: we need another thread. → Web Workers.</p>
    </PNotes>
  </WhoWins>
) : (
  <p-slide>
    <Image
      src={spongy}
      alt="SpongeBob meme: the problem and the solution"
      style="--size: 8em; border-radius: 0.3em"
    />
  </p-slide>
)}

<style>
  /* Credits under the event loop animation */
  figure {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 0;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-block-start: 0.8em;
    font-size: 0.3em;
    color: var(--soft-color);

    cite {
      font-style: normal;
    }
  }
</style>
